    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d615">

                <pb facs="0606" n="596" xml:id="pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Chile/61: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-30T17:00:00-04:00">December 30, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>851. The signature of the overall purchase agreement is merely awaiting approval
                    by Chilean Congress of copper tax proposal which the Minister of Finance hopes
                    may be forthcoming within the next few days. The Chilean authorities are very
                    anxious to close the agreement as soon as possible.<anchor n="88"
                        xml:id="d615-f1"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d615-f1" n="88" xml:id="d615-f1-content">
                <p>The agreement was completed by an exchange of notes on January 26, 1942.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
